<h2>Part 13. Frequently Asked Questions About Renting a 17 Seater Urbania</h2>

<h3>Seating and capacity</h3>
<p><strong>How many people can sit in a 17 seater Urbania?</strong> Up to 17 passengers plus the driver. We do not recommend carrying more, and we do not operate a larger Urbania.</p>
<p><strong>Can children share a seat?</strong> Each passenger has an individual captain seat. Very young children are best seated with an adult beside them. Tell us the number of children so we plan the seating sensibly.</p>
<p><strong>Do all the seats recline?</strong> The vehicle has recliner captain seats with calf and leg rests, so every passenger has their own recline.</p>
<p><strong>Is there a seat belt for every passenger?</strong> Seat belt fitment varies by seat. Ask us about the specific vehicle when you enquire, and wear belts wherever they are provided.</p>

<h3>Luggage</h3>
<p><strong>How much luggage fits?</strong> About 17 bags in the rear storage with a full group. Large hard-shell suitcases take more space than soft bags.</p>
<p><strong>Can I carry a cabin-size bag inside?</strong> Yes, small day bags can travel in the cabin with you.</p>

<h3>Pricing</h3>
<p><strong>What is the rate?</strong> ₹38 per km, with a 300 km daily minimum and ₹700 per day driver Bata.</p>
<p><strong>What is included?</strong> The rate covers the vehicle and the driver's time on the road. Tolls, parking, permits and state taxes are billed at actuals.</p>
<p><strong>Is there a fixed package price?</strong> Local city and airport trips are quoted per trip, in 8 hour/80 km and 12 hour/120 km packages. Outstation trips are billed on the per-km terms above.</p>
<p><strong>Can I get a GST invoice?</strong> Yes, on request.</p>
<p><strong>How do I pay?</strong> Payment terms are confirmed in the written quotation. Ask for them when you enquire.</p>

<h3>Trips and routes</h3>
<p><strong>Can I take the Urbania outside Karnataka?</strong> Yes. It runs to Tamil Nadu, Kerala, Andhra Pradesh and Goa. Interstate permits and state taxes are listed in the quotation.</p>
<p><strong>What if the trip extends longer than planned?</strong> Extra kilometres are billed at the same per-km rate, and extra Bata applies for duty beyond 10:00 PM. Tell the coordinator and the driver early if you plan to extend.</p>
<p><strong>Can the driver stay overnight at the destination?</strong> On multi-day trips the driver stays with the vehicle, and Bata is charged for each day of duty. Confirm any arrangement for the driver's stay in the quotation.</p>
<p><strong>What time can we start?</strong> Standard duty begins at 6:00 AM. If you need an earlier start, such as a pre-dawn departure for Tirupati, tell us when you enquire and we will confirm it in the quotation.</p>

<h3>Safety and service</h3>
<p><strong>Who drives the vehicle?</strong> An experienced, uniformed, commercial-badge chauffeur.</p>
<p><strong>Is the vehicle air-conditioned?</strong> Yes. The cabin has individual AC louvers above every seat.</p>
<p><strong>What if there is a problem on the road?</strong> Call our 24/7 support number at once, and the team will help you sort it out. Keep the driver's number and ours saved before you leave.</p>
<p><strong>What is the cancellation policy?</strong> Terms are confirmed at booking, and if we cancel a confirmed booking, any advance is refunded in full. Read the <a href="/cancellation-policy">cancellation policy</a>.</p>

<h3>Comparing options</h3>
<p><strong>Urbania or Tempo Traveller for 17 people?</strong> Choose the Tempo Traveller for the lowest cost and the Urbania for comfort on long trips and for VIP guests.</p>
<p><strong>Urbania or a 21 seater mini bus?</strong> The Urbania suits up to 17. For 18 to 21, choose the mini bus.</p>
<p><strong>Is there a 21 seater Urbania?</strong> No. The Force Urbania seats 17 at most.</p>
<p><strong>What about a 12 seater?</strong> For up to 12 people, see the <a href="/12-seater-urbania-for-rent-in-bangalore">12 seater Maharaja Urbania</a> or the lower-cost 12 seater Tempo Traveller.</p>

